Repo guide for AI (Cursor)

Purpose

- Make it fast to locate code, extend features, and avoid redundant searches.

Tech overview

- Frontend: SolidJS + Vite in `src/`
- Signalling: Go (Fiber + WebSocket + TURN via pion) in `signalling/`
- Transport: WebRTC data channel, discovery via WebSocket, TURN bootstrapped from signalling

Run locally

- Signalling (from `signalling/`):
  - Create `kabootar.toml` (copy `kabootar.example.toml`), update `listen_address`, `cors_endpoint`, TURN values
  - Build: `go build -o out/rendezvous ./cmd/signalling`
  - Run: `./out/rendezvous`
- Web app (from repo root):
  - `yarn install --frozen-lockfile`
  - Configure `src/config.ts`: set `secure`, `baseURL`, derived `httpScheme/wsScheme`
  - `yarn dev`

Where things are

- Frontend
  - `src/config.ts`: STUN list, `secure`, `baseURL`, `httpScheme`, `wsScheme`
  - `src/connection/room.ts`: main P2P logic
    - `Room.create` → POST `/room` then WS `/ws/:id?k=<mKey>&m=t`
    - `Room.joinDirect` → WS `/ws/:id?k=<cKey>&m=f`
    - First WS server message is `["-1", turnURL]`
    - `MasterHandler` creates offer, sends metadata then file chunks (16 KiB)
    - `ClientHandler` answers and downloads (Stream SW → Blob fallback)
  - `src/connection/discovery.ts`: WS `GET /discover?ip=<public-ip>`; handle add/remove notifications
  - `src/connection/ip.ts`: extracts public IP using STUN candidates
  - `src/downloader/*`: download strategies
  - Pages: `src/pages/Home.tsx` (create share), `src/pages/Discover.tsx` (LAN discovery + PIN), `src/pages/Share.tsx` (sender/receiver view)
  - Components: `PinEntryDialog`, `QRDialog`, `DiscoveredRoom`, buttons
- Signalling (Go)
  - Entry: `signalling/cmd/signalling/main.go`
  - Web init and routes: `signalling/web/web.go`
  - Core handler & routing: `signalling/web/handler.go`
  - WS guard: `signalling/web/signalling.go`
  - Room state: `signalling/web/room.go`
  - Protocol enums/utils: `signalling/web/protocol.go`
  - REST endpoints: `signalling/web/create_room.go` (POST /room), `signalling/web/discovery.go` (GET /room, WS /discover)
  - TURN bootstrap: `signalling/web/turn.go` (UDP TURN server, auth)
  - Config: `signalling/config/config.go` (+ `kabootar.toml`)

HTTP and WS API (quick reference)

- POST `/room` (body: `["t"|"f", ip?]`)
  - Response: `[roomID, mKey, cKey, name, pin, emoji]`
  - If body indicates public IP, room is discoverable for that IP
- GET `/room?id=<roomID>&pin=<pin>` → `[cKey]` (client retrieves key after PIN)
- WS `/ws/:room_id?k=<key>&m=t|f`
  - First server → client message: `["-1", turnHost:port]`
  - Server → Master
    - Join: `["0", clientID]`
    - Leave: `["1", clientID]`
    - Relay client signal: `["2", clientID, msg]`
  - Master → Server: `["0", clientID, msg]`
  - Server → Client: `["0", msg]`, Gone: `["1]`
  - Client → Server: `["0", msg]`
- WS `/discover?ip=<public-ip>`
  - Server → Client: add `["0", id, name, emoji]`, remove `["1", id]`

WebRTC specifics

- Data channel label: `"d"`
- Metadata (first message over data channel): JSON `[fileName, fileSize, roomName, emoji]` as ArrayBuffer
- Chunk size: 16 KiB, backpressure via `bufferedAmountLowThreshold`
- ICE servers: Google public STUN + dynamic TURN from server:
  - TURN URL sent via WS first message; username = roomID (master) / id (client), credential = `cKey`

Discovery flow (high level)

- Sender creates room → server may mark discoverable under sender public IP
- Discover page gets own public IP via STUN, opens `/discover` WS
- Server pushes rooms for that IP; receiver selects room, enters PIN; server returns `cKey`; receiver navigates to `/:id#k=<cKey>` and joins WS

Important constants/labels

- Channel label: `d`
- Config toggles: `secure`, `baseURL`, `httpScheme`, `wsScheme`
- Safari/iOS file size limit logic in `src/utils/browser.ts` (2GB)

Common tasks → where to edit

- Change server host/ports: `src/config.ts` + signalling `kabootar.toml`
- Add/alter WS message types: `signalling/web/protocol.go` + client handlers in `src/connection/room.ts`
- Modify discovery behavior: `signalling/web/discovery.go` + `src/connection/discovery.ts`
- Alter TURN behavior: `signalling/web/turn.go` and how TURN URL is consumed in `src/connection/room.ts`
- UI flow or routing: `src/pages/*.tsx` and `src/App.tsx`
- Downloader behavior: `src/downloader/*`

Conventions

- Messages are string arrays for compactness; keep indices consistent with enums in `signalling/web/protocol.go`
- Keep `Room` class as the single entry API for frontend P2P actions
- Prefer small composable components in `src/components/`
- Type additions go in `src/types/`

Checks before shipping

- Frontend builds: `yarn build`
- Signalling runs and CORS set correctly for FE origin
- `src/config.ts` points to correct host and (ws|http) scheme

Search hints

- “Where is X WS message handled?” → start at `signalling/web/protocol.go`, then `handler.go`, then `src/connection/room.ts`
- “How is discover add/remove emitted?” → `signalling/web/discovery.go` (notify) and `src/connection/discovery.ts`
- “How does file transfer start?” → data channel open → metadata → client sets up downloader → user clicks Start → client sends `"ready"` → master starts chunking
